1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,420
Our recipe book has a history in the
cloud now, but only we can see it.

2
00:00:04,566 --> 00:00:08,292
This episode is about sharing:
publishing to the gallery,

3
00:00:08,292 --> 00:00:13,574
forking someone else's work, and taking
in changes a friend proposes to ours.

4
00:00:13,785 --> 00:00:18,825
Publish to gallery, in the Cloud menu,
puts the latest cloud version on a public

5
00:00:18,825 --> 00:00:19,390
page.

6
00:00:19,469 --> 00:00:22,971
A description and a few tags
are how people will find it:

7
00:00:22,971 --> 00:00:28,259
search reads both, and every tag becomes
a link to everything else that shares it.

8
00:00:28,289 --> 00:00:30,209
There's no category to pick.

9
00:00:30,323 --> 00:00:33,363
The gallery works that out
from the tags and the name.

10
00:00:33,573 --> 00:00:35,983
Then the preview pages, up to six.

11
00:00:36,102 --> 00:00:39,563
The first one you tick becomes
the cover on the gallery card,

12
00:00:39,563 --> 00:00:41,912
and the cover page is ticked already.

13
00:00:42,010 --> 00:00:43,560
I'll add Tomato Soup.

14
00:00:43,999 --> 00:00:48,009
Publish draws the previews, uploads
them, and the book is live.

15
00:00:48,078 --> 00:00:52,165
Each preview is a real render of
the page, made in your browser,

16
00:00:52,165 --> 00:00:54,458
so a big project takes a moment.

17
00:00:54,677 --> 00:00:56,917
Here it is in the gallery, under New.

18
00:00:56,992 --> 00:00:59,592
Its page shows exactly what we chose.

19
00:00:59,655 --> 00:01:02,911
And because it's ours, there's
an Edit listing button,

20
00:01:02,911 --> 00:01:08,045
which changes the description, tags and
previews without publishing anything new.

21
00:01:08,254 --> 00:01:12,374
One thing to remember: the gallery
shows the version you published.

22
00:01:12,452 --> 00:01:16,732
Anything you save after that stays
private, until you publish again.

23
00:01:16,938 --> 00:01:18,628
Now someone else's work.

24
00:01:18,686 --> 00:01:21,880
Sam's meal planner could do
with brighter day titles.

25
00:01:22,016 --> 00:01:26,170
Signed in, its page offers one
more button: Fork this project.

26
00:01:26,377 --> 00:01:30,807
A fork is a copy in your own cloud
that remembers where it came from.

27
00:01:30,910 --> 00:01:33,970
It opens in the editor
like any other project.

28
00:01:34,176 --> 00:01:36,509
The Cloud menu knows the difference.

29
00:01:36,645 --> 00:01:41,071
It says this is forked from upstream,
with a link back to Sam's page,

30
00:01:41,071 --> 00:01:44,015
and it offers Propose changes to upstream.

31
00:01:44,224 --> 00:01:46,044
First, the change itself.

32
00:01:46,155 --> 00:01:49,985
In Templates, I'll open the Day
template and select its title.

33
00:01:50,032 --> 00:01:52,042
Orange, from the color picker.

34
00:01:52,152 --> 00:01:57,393
Then it has to be saved to the cloud,
because a merge request always proposes your

35
00:01:57,393 --> 00:02:00,392
latest save, never
what's only in this tab.

36
00:02:02,688 --> 00:02:07,721
Propose changes to upstream asks for a
title and a short note about what changed,

37
00:02:07,721 --> 00:02:08,468
and why.

38
00:02:08,512 --> 00:02:13,232
Sam will read it before he sees a single
page, so write it the way you'd want to

39
00:02:13,232 --> 00:02:14,132
receive it.

40
00:02:15,789 --> 00:02:18,909
That makes a merge request,
with a page of its own.

41
00:02:18,966 --> 00:02:22,782
It lists the changes, here one
template, and it waits for Sam:

42
00:02:22,782 --> 00:02:24,816
he can merge it, or close it.

43
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:27,030
It's his project, so it's his call.

44
00:02:27,239 --> 00:02:29,529
Meanwhile, Sam forked our book too.

45
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:32,847
He added a recipe, and
proposed it back to us.

46
00:02:32,947 --> 00:02:36,720
Merge requests for your projects
are listed on their gallery pages,

47
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:38,547
where only you can see them.

48
00:02:38,757 --> 00:02:43,827
Its page lists what changed: the page
hierarchy, because Sam added a page.

49
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:46,898
Render before and after
draws a page both ways,

50
00:02:46,898 --> 00:02:50,380
so you can see the change,
not just read about it.

51
00:02:50,591 --> 00:02:54,911
Merge makes a new version of our
project with Sam's recipe in it.

52
00:02:55,038 --> 00:02:56,358
It asks first.

53
00:02:56,855 --> 00:02:58,685
The merge happened in the cloud.

54
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:02,707
The book open in our editor hasn't
changed, and that's on purpose:

55
00:03:02,707 --> 00:03:05,540
nothing changes your
work behind your back.

56
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:10,100
Try to save, and the cloud says it
has moved on, and overwrites nothing.

57
00:03:13,896 --> 00:03:17,856
Reload cloud version brings the
merged book into the editor.

58
00:03:17,925 --> 00:03:22,705
And there's Sam's Shakshuka: on the
cover's index, and as a page of its own.

59
00:03:22,917 --> 00:03:26,397
Publish again whenever you want
the gallery to have it too.

60
00:03:26,447 --> 00:03:30,838
And that is the series: from a first
planner, to a book that people share and

61
00:03:30,838 --> 00:03:32,057
improve together.

62
00:03:32,136 --> 00:03:33,336
Thanks for watching.
